From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TeeJayBaker <Tom_John_baker@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 21:09:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] shader_split: Unity profile keys for the player's hardware
 tier and for variants and passes it never draws

Unity compiles each variant once per hardware tier and ships keyword variants whatever the scenes
enable. Overcooked! All You Can Eat (Unity 2019.4.11f1) splits to 520,394 shaders this way, 2.3 GB of
package and 293k pipeline pairs, a shader build of many hours.

Three optional profile keys, read by shader_split.py:
- unity_tier: keep only the programs of the tier the player runs (unity_code_blobs)
- unity_skip_keywords: leave out programs compiled with a keyword the game data never enables
  (unity_skipped, global or local keywords)
- unity_skip_passes: leave out passes by LightMode tag; META is drawn only by the editor's
  lightmapper (unity_pass_drawn)

Without the keys every program is read as before, so the committed tables of the other Unity
profiles split unchanged. Tests in dm/gfx/tests/test_unity_tier.py; the findings are in
docs/reference/shaders.md and the keys in dm/games/README.md.

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#836
Reason: Unity profile keys that leave out shader tiers, keyword variants and passes a game never draws
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#369

