+| `unity_tier` | `0`, `1` or `2` (every tier by default): `shader_split.py` keeps only the Unity programs of that hardware tier, the one the player runs ([Unity programs for every hardware tier](../../docs/reference/shaders.md#unity-programs-for-every-hardware-tier)) |
+| `unity_skip_keywords` | Unity keywords, space-separated (none by default): `shader_split.py` leaves out every Unity program compiled with one of them. Only for a keyword the game data shows is never enabled ([Unity variants and passes the player never draws](../../docs/reference/shaders.md#unity-variants-and-passes-the-player-never-draws)): a program the player asks for that is not built is not drawn |
+| `unity_skip_passes` | Pass `LightMode` tags, space-separated, any case (none by default): `shader_split.py` leaves out the programs of Unity passes with one of them. `META` is the one the player never draws ([Unity variants and passes the player never draws](../../docs/reference/shaders.md#unity-variants-and-passes-the-player-never-draws)) |
 | `shader_groups`, `shader_note` | `shader_split.py` source groups and the map header note (Engage: `engine` for `data.unity3d` and `Resources/`, `assets` for the Addressables bundles) |
 
